## What to capture

```jsx
// 1. Render errors — the component stack is the valuable part
class ErrorBoundary extends React.Component {
  static getDerivedStateFromError(error) { return { error }; }

  componentDidCatch(error, info) {
    Sentry.captureException(error, {
      contexts: { react: { componentStack: info.componentStack } },
    });
  }
  render() { return this.state.error ? this.props.fallback : this.props.children; }
}
```

```js
// 2. Async errors — error boundaries do NOT catch these
window.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => {
  Sentry.captureException(e.reason);
});

window.addEventListener('error', (e) => {
  Sentry.captureException(e.error ?? new Error(e.message));
});
```

The unhandled rejection handler is the one people forget, and async failures are the majority of real production errors.

